A library for communicating with Android radio services, built on top
of libgbinder.

It directly supports a number of known Android radio interfaces and can
be set up to work with custom (e.g. vendor specific) interfaces as long
as those interfaces work the same way, roughly like this:

        RadioRequest                RadioClientIndicationFunc
       ==============               =========================
         |         ^                           ^
      submit()     |                           |
         |         |                           |
         |      complete()                     |
         |         |                           |
  +------|---------|---------------------------|-----------+
  |      |         |     RadioInstance         |           |
  |      |    +=================+   +===================+  |
  |      |    | Response object |   | Indication object |  |
  |      |    | (resp_ifaces)   |   | (ind_ifaces)      |  |
  |      |    +=================+   +===================+  |
  |      |         ^                           ^           |
  +------|---------|---------------------------|-----------+
         |         |                           |
      Request      |                           |
    (serial, ...)  |                           |
         |         |                           |
  <------------------------- binder ----------------------->
         |         |                           |
         |       Response                      |
         |  (RadioResponseInfo, ...)           |
         |         |                           |
         v         |                           |
     +===================+                     |
     | (req_iface)       |----- Indication ----+
     | Radio service     |  (RadioResponseInfo, ...)
     +===================+

If some types and interfaces look strange to you, keep in mind that
this library was originally written for IRadio hidl interfaces and
later extended to support other things, too. Some legacy things had
to stay for backward compatibility.
